course: dictionary
lesson: 3496
title: Who is a farmer?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A farmer is a person who owns or works on a farm, growing crops or raising animals. Read the words around farmer to check. «Farmers cut the pods, scoop out the beans, and dry them in the sun» tells you that farmers grow and harvest food.
explain: Farmers do not work alone. «Before a loaf of bread reaches you, many people work on it: a farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes.» Each person has a different job, and the farmer's job comes first, at the start of the bread's journey.
explain: Farmers also work with the land and the weather. «Farmers in hilly places cut steps called terraces into the slopes, so the flat steps hold water and stop soil washing away.» Here the clues are soil, water and slopes, so a farmer must care for the ground as well as the crops.
fact: A farmer owns or works on a farm.
fact: Farmers grow crops, such as wheat, and raise animals.
fact: «Farmers in hilly places cut steps called terraces into the slopes» to hold water and stop soil washing away.
fact: «The Terracotta Army near Xi'an was found in 1974 by farmers digging a well.»
fact: Farmers' markets are places where you can buy food straight from the people who grew or raised it.
exercise: «A farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes.» Who grows the wheat? | a miller | a baker | a driver | *a farmer
exercise: «Farmers in hilly places cut steps called terraces into the slopes.» What do the farmers cut into the slopes? | a well | *steps called terraces | a road for cars | a stone wall around a castle
exercise: Maths: A farmer has 12 hens and sells 5 of them. How many hens does the farmer have left? | *7 | 17 | 6 | 8
test: Which job does a farmer do? | Sells cars in a showroom | Delivers letters to homes | Builds houses for families | *Grows crops or raises animals
test: Where might you buy food straight from a farmer? | At a bus stop | At a swimming pool | In a library | *At a farmers' market
exam: What is a farmer? | A tool for digging holes | A place where animals sleep | *A person who owns or works on a farm | A kind of crop
